pocket-motion-only: the inventory exists for a build that mounts the bundle it built, which is this repository's (`src/cli/build.ts`); it bakes `<Path>` outlines, which only 0042's PATH op draws.

0054 — `<Path>` outlines a mount computes, baked. A `d` the collector cannot
read where it is written — imported from another module, or built from data
at mount, as d3-shape's `line()(rows)` builds a chart's — was refused at
mount. A pocket-motion composition is mount-only, so every outline it will
draw is in the tree right after mount: the build mounts once, takes the keys
the tree asked for, bakes them, and mounts the result again.
`docs/text-shaping.design.md` proposed the same inventory for strings.

What the patch adds, by file:

- `framework/compiler/jsx-plugin.ts`: the collector records, as
  `unreadPaths`, every `d` attribute (and every one whose `viewBox` it
  cannot read) it records no outline for, with its line and column. The
  field rides in the transform cache entry, whose file is in the cache key.
- `tools/build.ts`: the build prints them on one line,
  `  paths at mount: N d attribute(s) not read by the build (file:line:col, …)`,
  which is what tells pocket-motion's `runBuild` to mount. And
  `--path-inventory=<file>` — `{ "outlines": [{ "d": [...], "viewBox"? }] }`
  — bakes those outlines AFTER the literal ones, deduplicated by key, so a
  build without the flag writes the bytes it wrote; one that does not bake
  is `error: <file>: outline N, computed at mount: <Path> d does not bake: …`.
- `framework/src/native-tree.ts`: `setPath`, on a key the build did not bake,
  hands it to `ui.__unbakedPath` when the host installs one and clears the
  node's outline; without one a strict host refuses it as before, its message
  now naming the mount inventory.

In this repository, `src/cli/build.ts` reads the line, mounts the bundle
through `src/render/path-inventory.ts`, writes `<output>.paths.json` beside
the pak, rebuilds with `--path-inventory=` (the argv `build.json` records)
and mounts again; a mount that asks for more is refused.

Red cases, run by `baselines/svg-import/redcheck.ts`, each an edit to one `+`
line of this patch (the harness rebuilds the vendored tree from the edited
patch and restores it) — or, for the last three, to `src/cli/build.ts` —
each turning the named test of `tests/path-inventory.test.ts` red:
- the collector does not report a d it cannot read -> -t a computed d and a forwarded prop are unread
- the build ignores --path-inventory -> -t a d computed at mount is baked from an inventory and draws
- an inventory outline that does not parse is not located -> -t does not parse is refused naming the inventory
- mount refuses an unbaked outline even with an inventory host -> -t a d computed at mount is baked from an inventory and draws
- runBuild never reads the paths-at-mount line -> -t a d computed at mount is baked from an inventory and draws
- runBuild does not mount the rebuilt bundle -> -t a mount that computes different outlines
- runBuild mounts and writes an inventory for every build -> -t every d is a literal is built once

The fixture is `compositions/data-chart`, in both ledgers: a line chart
whose rules, area, series and dots are computed at mount from rows in
another module, by a monotone cubic written with + - * / only.

`git apply` skips everything above the first `diff --git`.

